<title>FRANCE: Clinton, Yeltsin meet after Paris NATO summit.</title>
<headline>Clinton, Yeltsin meet after Paris NATO summit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. President Bill Clinton and Russian President Boris Yeltsin held a private meeting on Tuesday after signing an agreement founding a new partnership between Russia and NATO for security in Europe.</p>
<p>The two leaders met at the U.S. ambassador's residence in Paris. American officials said Clinton would seek clarification of Yeltsin's surprise announcement at a NATO-Russia summit that Moscow would no longer target nuclear weapons at the 16 member states of the Atlantic alliance.</p>
</text>
